cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or research in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Q-Net: Quantum Entanglement-Based Post-Internet Architecture"
abstract: >
  Q-Net is a conceptual framework and empirical proof-of-concept for a
  post-Internet communication architecture based on quantum state teleportation.
  This repository documents a 4-sprint hardware implementation on IBM Quantum
  systems (ibm_torino, ibm_fez, ibm_marrakesh), achieving a peak teleportation
  fidelity of 99.09% through iterative architectural improvements including
  static circuit design and hardware-aware transpilation.
